### Setup Test Users for Authentication
### ========================================================================
### Run these in order to create fresh test users with properly hashed passwords

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3002/api/v2/users


### ——— STEP 1: Check existing users ————————————————————————————————————
GET {{baseUrl}}


### ——— STEP 2: Delete old test users (if needed) ———————————————————————
### Replace with actual MongoDB _id from STEP 1
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/6a06cc4a416f03d890cbcf67


### ——— STEP 3: Create test user - Charlie ——————————————————————————————
POST {{baseUrl}}/hash
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "Charlie",
    "email": "charlie@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "role": "user"
}


### ——— STEP 4: Create test user - Admin ————————————————————————————————
POST {{baseUrl}}/hash
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "Admin User",
    "email": "admin@example.com",
    "password": "admin123",
    "role": "admin"
}


### ——— STEP 5: Verify users were created ———————————————————————————————
GET {{baseUrl}}


